          %h1#zorns_lemma Zorn's Lemma
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement_and_proofs"} Statement and proofs
              %li
                %a{:href => "#bourbakiwitt_theorem"} Bourbaki-Witt theorem
              %li
                %a{:href => "#wellordered_formulation"} Well-ordered formulation
              %li
                %a{:href => "#usageapplications"} Usage/applications
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em> Zorn's lemma
            , also known as Kuratowski-Zorn lemma, is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+theory"} order theory
            %em
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              in which every sub-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bound"} upper bound
              has a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal element
          %p
            Depending on the chosen perspective on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            this is either an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deduction"} consequence
            of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+excluded+middle"} axiom of excluded middle
            together imply the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
          %p
            In as far as it holds or is assumed to hold, Zorn’s lemma is a standard method for constructing (or at least,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proving
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existence"} existence
            of) objects that are ‘maximal’ in an appropriate sense. It is commonly used in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            and named after the algebraist
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Zorn"} Max Zorn
            (although he himself protested the naming after him).
          %h2#statement_and_proofs Statement and proofs
          #ChainAndUpperBound.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Given a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preordered
                  set
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ≤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \leq)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  is
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq x
                  whenever
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow S
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} total order
                  on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bound"} upper bound
                  of a subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  is an element
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \leq x
                  whenever
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in A
          #statement.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
              %strong Zorn's Lemma
              states that a preordered set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has a maximal element if every chain in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has an upper bound.
          #TheLemma.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Suppose the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds. Then Zorn's Lemma holds.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By contradiction. (We freely use the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+excluded+middle"} axiom of excluded middle
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              has no maximal element. Then every chain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subseteq S
              has a
              %em strict
              upper bound: an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \lt x
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is not maximal by supposition, so any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \lt x
              will serve.) For each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subseteq S
              that is well-ordered by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(W)
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Well
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: Well(S) \to S
              from well-ordered subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Well
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \in Well(S)
              is
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                \-inductive
              if for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in W
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                      %mo :
                      %mi y
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = f(\{y \in W: y \lt x\})
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Well
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y, Z \in Well(S)
              be
              = succeed "-inductive" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+set"} initial segment
              of the other. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be the union of all subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              that are initial segments of both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              and
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is maximal among such initial segments of both. Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is
              %em properly
              contained in both; let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              be the least element of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \setminus I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
